    "result_text": "All tests pass (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the suite, and the full `mvn test` build succeeds).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `namesakeCount` \u2014 the number of existing owners sharing the same firstName + lastName (case-insensitively) at the moment an owner is created \u2014 as a persisted, read-only field returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nI kept structural impact low by putting the new behaviour in small, cohesive units rather than growing any large method or class:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `namesakeCount` column field plus a small self-contained `assignNamesakeCount(Collection<Owner>)` that does the counting, alongside a getter/setter. The counting logic lives in its own tiny method, not inside an existing complex one.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 reused the existing `owner.isNew()` create branch (already used for `customerCode`), sharing the single `ownerRepository.findAll()` call so the method's complexity is unchanged (one added call, no new branch).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `namesakeCount` to the `Owner` schema as a read-only `int32`. The generated `OwnerDto` field is then mapped automatically by the existing MapStruct mapper (matching property name), so no mapper code changed.\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `namesake_count INTEGER` column (the profile the tests use; the app's h2 profile auto-updates DDL, matching how `customer_code`/`household_id` were handled).\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended the extra positional `NULL` to the 10 seed owner inserts to match the new column count.\n\nThe counting follows the same style as the existing `OwnerUniqueTelephoneAdvice`/`OwnerUniqueHouseholdAdvice` (case-insensitive comparison over the current owners), and because it runs while the new owner is still unpersisted, `findAll()` returns exactly the pre-create set \u2014 giving the \"before this create\" snapshot the spec requires.",
